JIT Core

JIT Core is a work in progress dynamic recompilation core for ARM, Thumb, and AArch64 instruction streams.

The current code contains the portable execution and instruction behavior layer for a 32-bit ARM and Thumb core and a 64-bit AArch64 core. It keeps register state, floating point state, vector state, status flags, program counters, and reservation state, and it dispatches supported instructions through Zig code.

Memory, exceptions, system behavior, cycle accounting, cache operations, and fallback handling are supplied by the host program through callbacks. JIT Core does not own the surrounding machine state or operating environment.

The project is still in active development.
